Notation: ℝ^k := Fin k → ℝ with the product Lebesgue measure L^k (volume); e_i := Pi.single i 1; Hᵐ := μHE[m]. Assume (PM) and (FTC) below.

(PM) is the exact frozen statement of the DAG theorem cbr_cipi_affine_plane_measure. For all P, m ∈ ℕ, every orthonormal w : Fin m → ℝ^P and every a ∈ ℝ^P, put S := {y : y − a ∈ span(range w)}. Then:
- (i) Measure.map (z ↦ a + Σ_i z_i w_i) Lᵐ = Hᵐ⌞S;
- (ii) S is closed;
- (iii) (Hᵐ⌞S)(K) < ∞ for every compact K;
- (iv) (Hᵐ⌞S)(B_r(a)) > 0 for every r > 0.

(FTC) is the exact frozen statement of the DAG theorem cbr_cipi_halfspace_partial_integral. For every d ∈ ℕ, every C¹ compactly supported g : ℝ^{d+1} → ℝ and every t ∈ ℝ:
- ∫_{z_0<t} Dg(z)(e_i) dz = 0 for every i ≠ 0;
- ∫_{z_0<t} Dg(z)(e_0) dz = ∫_{ℝ^d} g(Fin.cons t z′) dz′.

Conclusion. Let P, d ∈ ℕ, let v = (v_0, …, v_d) be an orthonormal family in ℝ^P, let φ ∈ TestFormOn univ d (smooth with compact support) and let t ∈ ℝ. Put V₀ := span(v_0, …, v_d) and L_t := {y : y − t v_0 ∈ span(v_1, …, v_d)}, where (v_1, …, v_d) = Fin.tail v. Then
∫_{V₀ ∩ {y : ⟨y, v_0⟩ < t}} dφ(y)(v_0, …, v_d) dH^{d+1}(y) = ∫_{L_t} φ(y)(v_1, …, v_d) dH^d(y).
